  "name": "late-head-then-compact-aged-after-commit",
  "note": "Built by hand from late-head-then-compact for 04 step 7 (phase F part 8b): a's head PUT is delayed and its commit fails while its packs are seconds old; then two 6 h 1 min jumps; then client 0's compact deletes a's packs as old orphans (a's session has ended: no horizon) and, with them, a's segment, older than T_idx and named by no head; then the late head lands. The segment goes with the packs, so the case shows LateHeadSegmentCollected (04 step 8), as LateHeadThenCompact's doc predicts. Since I8 a commit's packs are at most T_pack − M − 30 min old at its fence, so LateHeadThenCompact needs a jump of 40 to 60 min after the fence on top of 11 h 14 to 11 h 20 before it, which the driver's jumps (at most three of 61 s, 16 min, 46 min, 3 h 1 min, 6 h 1 min) cannot make: no seed shows it any more. Since 04 step 8 (phase F part 9) this runs on the fallback store, which keeps the hazard; late-head-then-compact-aged-after-commit-conditional is the same case on a conditional store.",
